xtra files, or refactors of unrelated pane code.\n- Record a short RUNLOG.md in `./runs/YYYY-MM-DD-cockpit-dark-mode/`, covering what changed, evidence, and any follow-ups. Park new ideas there instead of acting on them.\n\nDone when\n- The mod loads after `/reload-plugins` with no validation errors, and the validation output lists every hook and API call, including the new ones.\n- Using `/drive-screen`, screenshot the pane in both modes and confirm the toggle switches them and the choice persists after a reload. Save the screenshots in the run folder."}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"local_command_source":"<local-command-stdout>bws-enhance: Add a dark mode toggle to the cockpit pane in this mod project.\n\nContext\n- Find the cockpit pane first: search the mod's `hooks/` modules for its `ui.render` handler and for any `/cockpit` command registration. Don't assume file names. Use codegraph if `.codegraph/` exists.\n- Use `/plugin-authoring` and the generated `.claude-plugin/types/` declarations as the source of truth for `ui.render`, state, and invalidation signatures. They override online examples.\n- Assumption: \"dark mode\" means the pane's own palette switches between a dark and a light variant. Don't touch Claude Code's global theme or anything outside the pane. If the pane has no light/dark palette yet, define the minimum needed within the existing styling approach.\n\nScope\n- Add one toggle control with a stable id, wired to its event so clicking it flips the mode.\n- Redraw the pane when the mode changes, using the documented invalidation API.\n- Persist the choice. Use the storage that matches \"survives sessions\" per the state guide, and pick a sensible default. Mention the choice in your summary.\n- Keep the module statically inspectable: literal event names, direct `$.namespace.method(...)` calls, no aliasing or dynamic imports. Preserve `next` behavior for existing handlers.\n\nConstraints\n- Make only the changes asked. No n